  "cache:linkedin": {
    "entries": {
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4492437619": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-24T13:52:57.096884+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Description\nHBOX Digital is looking for an experienced React Native Mobile App Developer to join our development team.\nThe ideal candidate should have strong expertise in building, optimizing, and maintaining high-quality mobile applications for Android and iOS.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop and maintain cross-platform mobile applications using React Native.\nIntegrate REST APIs and third-party services.\nOptimize app performance, responsiveness, and user experience.\nTroubleshoot bugs and ensure application stability.\nCollaborate with UI/UX designers, backend developers, and project managers.\nPublish and maintain applications on Google Play Store and Apple App Store.\nRequirements\nMinimum 3+ years of professional experience in React Native development.\nStrong knowledge of JavaScript/TypeScript and React Native.\nExperience with REST APIs, Git, and state management libraries.\nFamiliarity with Android and iOS deployment processes.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nHow to Apply\nApply using the button on this page, apply through Indeed, or send your updated CV to hr@hboxdigital.com.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4492894790": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-24T13:52:57.096884+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nThe role focuses on building the customer-facing layer of the product: performant, accessible web applications used daily by thousands of active users. Day-to-day work spans React/TypeScript component architecture, state management, API integration, and the frontend build and deployment pipeline.\nThe frontend team sits at the intersection of design and engineering. The role directly shapes how features ship — collaborating with product managers and designers on scoping, prototyping, and delivering polished user experiences with measurable performance and quality standards.\nKey Responsibilities\nBuild and maintain complex, reusable React components in TypeScript, with a focus on accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA) and responsive design across breakpoints\nOwn feature delivery end-to-end: wire up GraphQL/REST APIs, manage client state (Redux Toolkit or equivalent), and ship behind feature flags\nOptimize application performance — bundle size, code splitting, Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) — using tooling like Lighthouse and Webpack/Vite\nWrite unit, integration, and end-to-end tests with Jest, React Testing Library, and Playwright; maintain CI gates on coverage and flakiness\nCollaborate with designers in Figma to translate mockups into pixel-accurate, component-driven UIs; contribute to and consume the internal design system\nParticipate in code reviews, pairing sessions, and architecture discussions; help establish frontend standards and documentation\nDebug and resolve production issues using Sentry, Datadog RUM, and browser dev tools; own root-cause analysis for frontend incidents\nWhat We Are Looking For\n3–6 years of professional frontend engineering experience building and shipping production web applications\nDeep proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React (hooks, context, suspense patterns), and modern CSS (Tailwind, CSS-in-JS, or CSS Modules)\nHands-on experience with client state management (Redux Toolkit, Zustand, or React Query) and consuming REST and GraphQL APIs\nTrack record of improving measurable frontend performance metrics in a production environment\nStrong testing discipline: comfortable writing and maintaining unit and E2E test suites in CI/CD pipelines\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience\nBonus: Experience with Next.js or server-side rendering, Storybook-driven component development, or contributing to an open-source design system",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4493108186": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-24T13:52:57.096884+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About The Role\nThe role owns the user-facing surface of the product - React and TypeScript applications serving hundreds of thousands of daily users, where load performance, accessibility, and interaction quality directly drive retention and revenue.\nYou will work alongside product designers and backend engineers to ship features end-to-end, with ownership of component architecture, state management patterns, and frontend build tooling.\nKey Responsibilities\nBuild and maintain production React applications using TypeScript, Next.js, and modern state management (Redux Toolkit, TanStack Query, or Zustand)\nShip responsive, accessible interfaces that meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards and pass rigorous cross-browser and mobile testing\nInstrument and optimize Core Web Vitals - bundle splitting, lazy loading, render performance - using tools like Lighthouse, Sentry, and Datadog RUM\nDesign and maintain a shared component library in Storybook, ensuring design consistency and reducing duplication across product surfaces\nCollaborate with backend engineers on API contract design, contributing to OpenAPI specifications and building strongly-typed client SDKs\nWrite unit and end-to-end tests with Jest, React Testing Library, and Playwright as part of a CI/CD pipeline with high deployment frequency\nParticipate in architecture reviews, code reviews, and frontend guild discussions that raise the bar for the broader engineering team\nWhat We Are Looking For\n3–7 years of frontend engineering experience building consumer- or enterprise-scale web applications\nDeep proficiency in JavaScript/TypeScript, React, and modern CSS architecture (CSS Modules, Tailwind, or CSS-in-JS)\nExperience with at least one modern meta-framework: Next.js, Remix, or Vite-based setups with SSR/SSG\nTrack record of shipping measurable performance improvements (LCP, INP, bundle size) in production environments\nStrong grasp of browser internals: rendering pipeline, network waterfall, caching, and async patterns\nBachelor's degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience\nBonus: Experience with design systems (Figma token workflows), WebSockets/real-time UIs, or React Native; contributions to open-source frontend tooling",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-24T13:52:57.096884+00:00"
  },
